 ## Background
-The technique was introduced as 'Sphere Tracing' by John C. Hart in 1996 in 'Sphere tracing: a geometric method for the antialiased ray tracing of implicit surfaces' [S8]. It was also referenced in Hart's 1989 work 'Ray Tracing Deterministic 3-D Fractals' and NVIDIA Gems2 (2004) [S8].
-It became widely used in 4k intros released in 2009, specifically in productions like 'Frequency' by xt95 and 'Potatro' [S17, unofficial]. It is widely used in real-time shader art (e.g., Shadertoy) for rendering scenes with no mesh data, and for volumetrics (fog, clouds) by treating density as an SDF [S3, unofficial].
